Vendored subset of the Wuffs library, used by Python/pystrtod.c for
string-to-float conversion (replaces _Py_dg_strtod from Python/dtoa.c).

Upstream:    https://github.com/google/wuffs
Version:     v0.4 amalgamated single-file release
Commit:      126a80a (main branch at time of drop, 2026-04-21)
License:     Apache-2.0 OR MIT (dual; see LICENSE-APACHE)

Files included:

    wuffs-v0.4.c    — single-file amalgamated Wuffs release. Despite the
                      .c extension, this doubles as both the header and
                      the implementation — see WUFFS_IMPLEMENTATION
                      below.
    LICENSE-APACHE  — upstream dual-license text

Size note. The amalgamated source is ~3.3 MB because it ships every
Wuffs module (image codecs, JSON, compression, etc.). We only compile in
the `base` module's `floatconv` sub-module by defining

    WUFFS_CONFIG__STATIC_FUNCTIONS
    WUFFS_CONFIG__MODULES
    WUFFS_CONFIG__MODULE__BASE
    WUFFS_CONFIG__MODULE__BASE__CORE
    WUFFS_CONFIG__MODULE__BASE__FLOATCONV
    WUFFS_CONFIG__MODULE__BASE__INTCONV
    WUFFS_IMPLEMENTATION

in the TU that compiles wuffs-v0.4.c. Unused modules become empty after
the preprocessor pass; the resulting object file is ~80–100 KB.

The actual bridge between Wuffs and CPython is Python/_wuffs/wuffs_strtod.c,
which wraps wuffs_base__parse_number_f64 behind an extern _Py_wuffs_strtod
entry point matching the old _Py_dg_strtod calling convention (takes an
ASCII C string, returns a double, writes the end-of-parse pointer into
*endptr, sets errno = ERANGE on over/underflow).

Updating:

    curl -L -o Python/_wuffs/wuffs-v0.4.c \
        https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/wuffs/<SHA>/release/c/wuffs-v0.4.c
    curl -L -o Python/_wuffs/LICENSE-APACHE \
        https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/wuffs/<SHA>/LICENSE

Then update this file's commit line.
